<p>Chile inaugurated José Antonio Kast as president on Wednesday, marking a peaceful transfer of power from outgoing leftist leader Gabriel Boric at the National Congress in Valparaíso. Multiple outlets called it Chile’s sharpest shift to the right since the country’s return to democracy in 1990, with Kast widely described as the most conservative head of state in decades. Kast cast the start of his administration as an “emergency government,” saying he was inheriting a country in worse shape than expected, and he pointed to security, the economy, and immigration as top priorities. As he left La Moneda for the last time, Boric wished the incoming government well and urged unity after tensions linked to a dispute over a Chinese undersea cable in the final weeks of his term.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/41YbJHFB03nsCOpWWRzSZKRbvWtb9sTAHzwMskztFeRSMf-kkcSQ0cg3yLiPT1rQVbJvyuxjFuQ5OV0xA5lrCWoUuEYAFeUBVL5bFT1_kiBFl4PG7SGItEN-lCkKRCbKdVqYYrnVYQAyl88yKGmbT4L2UxEYe5qUVsfUE31H8g' alt='José Antonio Kast during Chile’s presidential inauguration.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ceremony details: Senate President Paulina Núñez administered Kast’s oath and placed the presidential sash on him at the ceremony in Valparaíso.</li><li>Profile detail: El País described Kast, 60, as a lawyer as he took office.</li><li>Boric’s farewell setting: The South China Morning Post said Boric delivered his unity-and-success message from La Moneda’s courtyard and arrived with his partner, Paula.</li><li>Post-ceremony move: MercoPress reported that after Congress swore him in, Kast headed to the presidential palace, where he defended the idea of an “emergency government”.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President José Antonio Kast: Speaking after the ceremony, Kast defended launching an “emergency government,” saying he was receiving “a country in worse conditions than we could have imagined.” (<a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/12/chile-s-new-era-with-kast-in-power'>MercoPress</a>)</li><li>Outgoing President Gabriel Boric: In his farewell from La Moneda, Boric wished the incoming administration well and urged Chileans to put the country first: “I wish success to the incoming government, success for Chile, and may our homeland always come first, above any interest, above any disagreement.” (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3346275/chiles-boric-leaves-office-calls-unity-after-split-successor-over-china-cable'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>El País analysis: El País highlighted the symbolism of Kast’s presidential sash, saying it included an embroidered coat of arms—an institutional symbol it reported no leader had incorporated since the return to democracy, and one last used by Augusto Pinochet. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-11/chile-begins-its-most-conservative-era-with-kasts-emergency-government.html'>El País</a>)</li><li>NPR profile: NPR emphasized biographical context, tying Kast’s ideology to his upbringing in a small Andean town as part of explaining his rise to the presidency. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/11/nx-s1-5743653/chile-turns-right-kast-inaugurated-as-nations-most-conservative-leader-since-pinochet'>NPR</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-11/chile-begins-its-most-conservative-era-with-kasts-emergency-government.html'>Chile begins its most conservative era with Kast’s ‘emergency government’</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/12/chile-s-new-era-with-kast-in-power'>Chile&#x27;s new era with Kast in power</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3346275/chiles-boric-leaves-office-calls-unity-after-split-successor-over-china-cable'>Chile’s Boric leaves office, calls for unity after split with successor over China cable</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/kast-office-chile-marks-sharpest-shift-dictatorship-130957821'>Kast to take office as Chile marks its sharpest shift to the right since dictatorship</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/11/nx-s1-5743653/chile-turns-right-kast-inaugurated-as-nations-most-conservative-leader-since-pinochet'>Chile turns right: Kast inaugurated as nation&#x27;s most conservative leader since Pinochet</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/jose-antonio-kast-sworn-in-as-chiles-president-in-sharpest-shift-to-the-right-since-pinochet'>José Antonio Kast sworn in as Chile&#x27;s president, in sharpest shift to the right since Pinochet</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/03/11/chile-kast-inauguration-new-administration/f90f47d0-1d06-11f1-a29c-fd43da9a479a_story.html'>José Antonio Kast is sworn in as President of Chile, succeeding Gabriel Boric.</a> - washingtonpost.com</li></ul>